<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Agriculture details 1997 seeding plan.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Agriculture details 1997 seeding plan.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Agriculture on Tuesday detailed farmers' seeding intentions based on estimates provided by 300 area reporters across the province.</p>
<p>CROP    1997 planned    1996 Actual    Pct of 96  1987-96 Avg</p>
<p>w.wheat	90,000 ac     110,000 ac   82		162,000</p>
<p>s.wheat  13,500,000     14,470,000	93	   14,977,000</p>
<p>durum     4,600,000	4,250,000     108	    4,132,600</p>
<p>oats	2,100,000	2,150,000	98	    1,388,000</p>
<p>barley    4,700,000	4,800,000	98	    3,841,900</p>
<p>fall rye    170,000	  230,000	74		383,000</p>
<p>spring rye   20,000	   20,000     100		 42,200</p>
<p>flax	1,000,000	  870,000     115		729,000</p>
<p>canola    5,000,000	4,000,000     125	    4,160,900</p>
<p>mustard     510,000	  480,000     106		397,300</p>
<p>sunflower sd 20,000	   20,000     100		 28,900</p>
<p>lentils     710,000	  710,000     100		518,300</p>
<p>field pea 1,000,000	  920,000     109		568,600</p>
<p>canary sd   400,000	  490,000	82		297,000</p>
<p>TOTAL:   33,820,000     33,520,000     101	   31,627,000</p>
<p>fallow   10,700,000     11,000,000	97	   13,531,700</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
